From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v0lumehi <aljic.zijad@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:16:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iOS: quit a game from the touch controls or by holding Home
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On the iPhone a running game had no way back to the launcher: the
player had to close the app in the app switcher. Two ways now open a
quit prompt over the game, the Mac's (home_quit_mac.h) in look: "Quit
<game>?", a note, and Quit and Cancel pills of one fixed width in every
language.

- The touch controls get a quit control, a small × in the top row left
  of − (DmPadGeometry.h). It moves no other control, and its grab area
  stays clear of the grab areas of −, the layout button, L3, ZL and L
  on every screen and size. A tap opens the prompt, so a stray touch
  costs one more tap and never quits. DM_TOUCH_EXIT=0 hides it.
- Holding a controller's Home button for 2 s opens it too, as on the
  Mac (home_quit.h). The host already claims Home. iOS 27 respects the
  claim when the Home button setting for apps lets the app decide, and
  the log names the setting once. While a controller hides the touch
  controls the × stays, unless that setting lets the app decide, so a
  controller player always has a way out.

A tap on Quit or A quits. A tap on Cancel or outside the card, B or a
new press of Home closes it. While it is open the game is told it lost
the focus and gets no input, as on the Mac.

Quitting ends the process. One game runs per process (ShellMain.m), so
the engine cannot hand the window back to the shell's library. The
cloud saves go out as when the app goes to the background, then the
host ends as on SIGTERM (dm_host_shutdown). iOS cannot start an app
again by itself: the player opens it and the shell shows its library.
DM_HOME_QUIT_TEXT carries the texts, as on the Mac.

quit_prompt.h is Core Animation and Core Text only, so
tests/quit_prompt checks its layout, hits and touch steps on the Mac in
six languages and can draw it to PNGs (QP_CAPTURE_DIR).

Upstream-Status: pending (on 0065, seedds/nxnative#1084)
Reason: Players on the iPhone need a way back to the launcher from a running game: a touch quit control and the Home hold (#421)
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#421

