+// Two ways open the quit prompt (quit_prompt.h) over the game: the touch gamepad's quit control (a tap on the × at the top, DmGamepad.m), and holding a controller's
+// Home button for 2 seconds (home_quit.h, as on the Mac; the indicator at the top fills while it is held). A tap on Quit or A quits, a tap on Cancel or outside the
+// card, B or a new press of Home closes it. While it is open the game is told it lost the focus, as the Switch's HOME menu does, and gets no touch or controller input.
+// Quitting ends the process: one game runs per process (dm_profile() and the host's early loading run once, ShellMain.m), so the engine cannot hand the
+// window back to the shell's library and start another game. It goes the way of a SIGTERM (dm_host_shutdown: audio and graphics stopped, in-flight GPU work
+// drained, _exit(0)), after the cloud saves have gone out as they do when the app goes to the background. What the game saved is on disk already (hle_fs.c
+// writes each commit), progress it did not save is lost, as the prompt says. iOS has no way for an app to start itself again: the player opens it from the Home
+// Screen, and the shell opens on its library with this game first (the last played). DM_HOME_QUIT=0 turns the Home hold off, DM_TOUCH_EXIT=0 the quit control.
+// DM_HOME_QUIT_TEXT carries the texts in the player's language, one per line (home_quit.h's order), English otherwise.
